1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,771
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:31,448
<i>Red Dragon declared war on Lily Cruz,</i>
<i>and she needs her best lieutenant.</i>

6
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:33,491
[Damian] <i>Your lives are in danger, Camia.</i>

7
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:36,077
<i>I need to save you from Red Dragon.</i>

8
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:38,455
[Paterno] <i>I would like you to</i>
<i>meet Miss Mercedes' associate.</i>

9
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:39,873
<i>You!</i>

10
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:41,332
<i>Stop her!</i>

11
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:43,543
<i>Where's the bomb?!</i>

12
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:47,005
<i>Call the bomb squad,</i>
<i>and evacuate the building.</i>

13
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:48,423
<i>Do you understand?</i>

14
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:52,594
<i>Make sure everyone</i>
<i>gets out of this building!</i>

15
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:54,929
[Emilia] <i>I came here</i>
<i>because I wanted to know</i>

16
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,931
<i>if Mama had anything to do</i>

17
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:58,725
<i>with the bombing at Aguas Realty.</i>

18
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:00,935
<i>You'll find out soon enough.</i>
<i>When it's the right time.</i>

19
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:02,979
<i>Sir. Ma'am.</i>

20
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:05,190
<i>Sir Arnaldo's gone missing from his room!</i>

21
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:06,691
<i>We've searched the premises.</i>

22
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:10,070
<i>Order all of our men to move</i>
<i>if you have to.</i>

23
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:12,155
<i>Governor, we don't have</i>
<i>full access to that, as of now.</i>

24
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:14,991
<i>The one time we need to find Arnaldo,</i>

25
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,159
<i>and you're basically powerless.</i>

26
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:17,368
<i>What can you do? Nothing!</i>

27
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:18,828
<i>You are no longer in position,</i>

28
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:21,122
<i>so that's why you cannot do anything now!</i>

29
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:23,166
[Lily] <i>We can't let things end here.</i>

30
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:25,043
<i>If that Myla still refuses to talk,</i>

31
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:27,253
<i>then we'll gather information on our own.</i>

32
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:29,756
<i>Madam, we cleaned up the mess.</i>

33
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,716
[Diego] <i>He's dead. He was strangled.</i>

34
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,968
[Lily] <i>For now, let's hurry up</i>
<i>and find a lead.</i>

35
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:37,138
<i>"Mercedes Palacio"?</i>

36
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,688
[Paterno] <i>I also know of an investor</i>

37
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:47,565
<i>who's interested</i>
<i>in investing in Aguas Realty.</i>

38
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:49,818
<i>I would like you to meet</i>
<i>Miss Mercedes' associate.</i>

39
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:50,944
[Lily] <i>You!</i>

40
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:53,863
<i>You're the one who blew up</i>
<i>the media complex!</i>

41
00:01:53,947 --> 00:01:55,323
<i>That's right!</i>

42
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:58,159
<i>And I'm here to finish what I started!</i>

43
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:06,417
[tense music playing]

44
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:19,681
Let's go, Diego.

45
00:02:20,598 --> 00:02:22,016
Call the police.

46
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,101
Okay.

47
00:02:28,189 --> 00:02:29,190
Hurry.

48
00:02:31,109 --> 00:02:33,278
[tense music playing]

49
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:37,365
[Anna] U, V…

50
00:02:39,117 --> 00:02:40,285
W…

51
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:45,331
X, Y, and Z.

52
00:02:45,415 --> 00:02:47,041
Very good!

53
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:50,545
Okay. Take your seat, Angel.

54
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:54,841
All right.
Just continue what you're doing,

55
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:57,927
and later, we'll have
a little exercise, okay?

56
00:02:58,011 --> 00:02:59,554
-[kids] Yes, ma'am.
-Okay.

57
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,745
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

58
00:03:23,828 --> 00:03:25,455
<i>Please try again later.</i>

59
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:28,166
[man] Good morning, universe!

60
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:33,796
[tense music playing]

61
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:40,970
[Arnaldo] Oh, what a lovely day!

62
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:43,097
You know what?

63
00:03:43,723 --> 00:03:47,393
You're all the reason
why my mornings are so great.

64
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:51,105
You make me feel great! Especially you!

65
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:55,902
I know you give me clean air.
So, thank you.

66
00:04:01,532 --> 00:04:02,617
Lea?

67
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:10,875
Wasn't that hut abandoned?

68
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:12,335
[Lea] Yeah, as far as I know.

69
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:14,629
Do you know that guy standing over there?

70
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:17,215
[Lea] No. I've never seen him before.

71
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:18,883
-Okay, thanks anyway.
-All right.

72
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:20,551
-Please get back to the kids.
-Okay.

73
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:29,352
You're so beautiful. Just look at you.

74
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:31,688
What happened to your flowers?
Let me fix them up.

75
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:35,149
[tense music playing]

76
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:37,151
Just continue what you're doing.

77
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:40,571
Because you're making the people
who live here so happy.

78
00:04:40,655 --> 00:04:41,614
Especially me!

79
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:45,243
[tense music continues]

80
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:52,500
You too! You're the biggest one here.

81
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:55,211
You're being a great example
to all of them.

82
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:04,804
[tense music swelling]

83
00:05:04,887 --> 00:05:05,847
[exhales]

84
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:07,056
Good morning to everyone!

85
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:08,433
What a lovely day!

86
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:25,742
[reporter] <i>A woman hanged herself</i>

87
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,327
<i>in Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

88
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:30,621
<i>She was later identified</i>
<i>as Carlotta Navarro,</i>

89
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:33,791
<i>caretaker of businesswoman Ivy Aguas.</i>

90
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,543
[Anna] <i>Nanny Carlotta was like</i>
<i>a mother to me too.</i>

91
00:05:35,626 --> 00:05:37,211
<i>Please don't deny me the chance</i>

92
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:39,255
<i>to seek justice for her death.</i>

93
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:41,466
[Arnaldo] <i>I can kill you and make it look</i>

94
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:43,134
<i>like you committed suicide,</i>

95
00:05:43,217 --> 00:05:44,802
<i>just like what I did to Carlotta.</i>

96
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:47,180
[Anna] <i>Do you know how long I've waited</i>

97
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,806
<i>for this opportunity?</i>

98
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:51,768
<i>Anna.</i>

99
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:56,898
[breathing heavily]

100
00:06:03,571 --> 00:06:06,115
Arnaldo, you monster!
Of all the places I'd see you!

101
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:11,871
Ah, good morning, friend.

102
00:06:11,954 --> 00:06:13,581
-Friend? You monster!
-Wait! Hold on!

103
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:14,832
-You're a murderer!
-Hold on, hold on!

104
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,167
-What are you talking about?!
-Give me that!

105
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:17,502
-Hey! No.
-Give me that.

106
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:18,795
-Give me that.
-No, give it to me.

107
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:20,546
-I don't know--Give it to me.
-[Anna grunts]

108
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,965
-Hey! Are you all right?
-Don't touch me!

109
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:24,801
[Arnaldo] Uh--

110
00:06:24,884 --> 00:06:25,843
[pants]

111
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:30,264
[pensive music swelling]

112
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:35,520
-You look hurt. Let me see.
-No.

113
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:37,438
-I just want to--
-No!

114
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:38,898
Stay away from me!

115
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:42,985
[pensive music playing]

116
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:44,612
[Anna gasps]

117
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:45,863
[wood clatters]

118
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:50,910
You seem to know who I am.

119
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:52,995
I know you well enough!

120
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:54,956
You're Arnaldo Ardiente!

121
00:06:57,041 --> 00:06:58,042
Uh…

122
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:02,463
Good for you. I don't even know who I am.

123
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:05,675
[Anna gasps]

124
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:08,261
-Stay away!
-I won't hurt you.

125
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:10,263
-Don't come near me!
-I won't hurt you.

126
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,685
You see…

127
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:19,939
I don't know what you were talking about.

128
00:07:21,274 --> 00:07:22,608
I don't remember anything.

129
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:24,861
I don't know what happened,

130
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,404
but I've been told that I got sick,

131
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:31,409
so I can't remember a thing now.

132
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:40,001
People keep telling me of all
the wrong things I've done.

133
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:45,715
So if you're one of the people…

134
00:07:47,884 --> 00:07:50,136
that I've wronged before…

135
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:54,140
I want to ask for forgiveness.

136
00:07:55,975 --> 00:07:57,351
I hope you can forgive me.

137
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,653
-[Camia] Does it hurt?
-[Anna] No.

138
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:13,159
-There you go.
-Thank you, Auntie.

139
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:14,327
[Camia] It's nothing.

140
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:18,706
Anna, what happened to you?

141
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,751
She just tripped earlier, Jepoy.

142
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:27,381
And you? Where were you?
We were all worried.

143
00:08:27,465 --> 00:08:29,008
I've been trying to contact you.

144
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:30,593
Where have you been?

145
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:32,637
Going around town.

146
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:36,140
You should've been more careful.

147
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:53,533
-[Camia] It's done.
-[Anna] Thanks, Auntie.

148
00:08:57,662 --> 00:09:00,206
Lily, Diego, how did it go?

149
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:03,834
We need to be cautious, Mom.

150
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:05,711
[tense music playing]

151
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:07,630
I'm not dealing with just anybody.

152
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,174
Mr. Paterno's dead.

153
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:12,343
But I got a lead.

154
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,887
Mercedes Palacio.

155
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:17,181
[eerie music]

156
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:19,225
I'll find out who that monster is.

157
00:09:19,308 --> 00:09:23,980
[suspenseful music playing]

158
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:32,613
[Mercedes] <i>All you need to know right now</i>

159
00:09:32,697 --> 00:09:35,283
<i>is that Red Dragon declared war</i>
<i>on Lily Cruz.</i>

160
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:38,160
<i>And she needs her best lieutenant-- you.</i>

161
00:09:39,328 --> 00:09:42,582
[tense music playing]

162
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:52,675
Camia, you need to stop Lily.
This is serious!

163
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:55,553
Lily knows what she's doing, Damian.

164
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:59,432
They nearly blew her up.
How are you fine with that?

165
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:02,977
Lily's survived so much worse than that.

166
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,813
These people are on a different level.

167
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:07,315
She can't win this.

168
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:09,567
Why, Damian?

169
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:12,486
Do you know Mercedes Palacio?

170
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:15,281
No, I don't know her.

171
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:17,867
But they've shown us all

172
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:21,954
that they have the firepower
to bring her down.

173
00:10:22,413 --> 00:10:24,373
I know you're worried for my daughter.

174
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:27,501
But you have to trust her.

175
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:39,555
Camia, you need to fear them.

176
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:44,894
Because Lily's already standing
in her own grave.

177
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:54,320
[Lily] We need to leave now.
Mercedes Palacio took the bait.

178
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:59,408
She thinks someone's going
to inquire about her business.

179
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:01,535
But it's just going to be a ruse.

180
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:03,204
Don't worry.

181
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:05,665
Diego and the guards will be there.

182
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:07,416
Keep your eyes open, dear.

183
00:11:08,292 --> 00:11:09,585
I will. Thanks, Mom.

184
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:10,878
-Bye.
-Lily.

185
00:11:15,257 --> 00:11:16,342
What is it?

186
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:19,762
Be careful out there.

187
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:24,475
Mom.

188
00:11:27,853 --> 00:11:30,648
[pensive music playing]

189
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:48,374
[acoustic music playing]

190
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:09,603
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I want you to be happy.</i>

191
00:12:10,312 --> 00:12:13,941
<i>I want you to be free of this burden.</i>

192
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:16,610
<i>And I hope I'll be there with you.</i>

193
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:20,948
<i>You know how much I love you, right?</i>

194
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:23,325
[Ivy] <i>Diego, I love you.</i>

195
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:29,457
["Hindi Kita Iiwan" playing]

196
00:12:56,233 --> 00:12:58,152
Mercedes is on her way.

197
00:12:58,235 --> 00:12:59,862
My people are ready.

198
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:03,240
[romantic instrumental playing]

199
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,879
It's like there's no end to this fight.

200
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:20,591
[music continues]

201
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:53,457
[tense music playing]

202
00:13:57,586 --> 00:13:58,837
That's Mercedes.

203
00:13:59,755 --> 00:14:00,798
Standby, everyone.

204
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:05,427
[phone ringing]

205
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:07,179
Madam?

206
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:16,647
No. [scoffs] I wasn't aware.

207
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:18,566
I apologize.

208
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:21,735
Right away, Madam. Thank you.

209
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:25,364
Change of plans.
Turn the car around. Hurry!

210
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:29,952
What's going on?

211
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:33,873
Why is she turning the car around?

212
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:42,006
[Diego] What's she doing?

213
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:53,767
Let's go.

214
00:14:53,851 --> 00:14:58,898
[tense music playing]

215
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:07,656
Make sure to guard the house
and check the security--

216
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,575
She was right there, and we lost her!

217
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:14,622
Lily, how did it go?

218
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:16,123
It didn't push through, Mom.

219
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:19,043
Mercedes Palacio suddenly backed out.

220
00:15:19,126 --> 00:15:21,420
She literally went the other way.

221
00:15:22,004 --> 00:15:24,006
It's like she figured out we were waiting.

222
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:27,885
But this isn't over yet.

223
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:29,720
I will stop her.

224
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:34,099
She'll pay for everything she did to me.

225
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:55,537
Does it still hurt?

226
00:15:57,706 --> 00:15:59,500
No. I just don't want to overwork it.

227
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:03,879
What happened to you?

228
00:16:04,588 --> 00:16:08,175
I thought you had bodyguards.
None of them helped you out?

229
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:10,970
I was alone when this happened.

230
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:13,639
Why were you alone?

231
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:17,643
Don't be so stubborn, Anna.

232
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:21,146
You're in danger as long
as the Ardientes are out there.

233
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:24,358
I know, Jepoy. But I tripped
because I saw Arnaldo.

234
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:26,568
Arnaldo?

235
00:16:27,152 --> 00:16:28,153
[Jepoy mumbles]

236
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:34,326
Anna, be honest with me.
Did Arnaldo do that to you?

237
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:35,327
-No.
-Did he hurt you?

238
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:36,328
-No, Jepoy.
-He didn't hurt me.

239
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:37,329
Tell me the truth.

240
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:38,998
He didn't do anything to me.

241
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,750
Actually, it seems like he's changed.

242
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,419
[Jepoy] What do you mean?

243
00:16:44,962 --> 00:16:48,090
Anna, a snake may shed its skin,
but it's still a snake.

244
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:51,218
Do you think I'm stupid?
I know how dangerous he is.

245
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:52,636
And I thought the same way too.

246
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,806
But when I saw him,
the way he moved and spoke…

247
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:58,684
-He seemed crazy.
-He always was.

248
00:16:58,767 --> 00:17:00,394
That's not what I mean, Jepoy.

249
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:02,855
He said he doesn't remember
being an Ardiente.

250
00:17:02,938 --> 00:17:03,939
[Jepoy scoffs]

251
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:10,988
Anna, if the Devil himself
forgot he was a demon…

252
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:14,533
would you forgive him for all his sins?

253
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:18,245
I will never, ever forget
that he was the one

254
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:19,955
who killed Nanny Carlotta.

255
00:17:21,623 --> 00:17:23,625
But, when I saw him, it was like…

256
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,420
it was like he was innocent!

257
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:29,423
Jepoy, can you actually
punish someone for a crime

258
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:30,924
they don't remember committing?

259
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:35,763
[Jepoy] I'll kill him.

260
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:40,267
[suspenseful music playing]

261
00:18:06,293 --> 00:18:07,878
[Julio] <i>Is everything all right?</i>

262
00:18:07,961 --> 00:18:10,005
<i>Of course, Grandpa.</i>
<i>Everything's all right.</i>

263
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,381
<i>I've never felt better.</i>

264
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:14,384
<i>You know, it's like a heavy load</i>

265
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:15,969
<i>was lifted from my heart.</i>

266
00:18:18,972 --> 00:18:20,641
[Ivy] <i>I want to quit politics, Grandpa.</i>

267
00:18:20,724 --> 00:18:22,351
-<i>I want to be a priest.</i>
-[chokes]

268
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,449
[Emilia] Hmm…

269
00:18:39,076 --> 00:18:43,455
So, how does it feel
to be powerless, Papa?

270
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:49,336
Do you feel now what you made me
feel all these years?

271
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:54,216
Why, Emilia?

272
00:18:54,758 --> 00:18:57,386
What do you have to pride yourself on?

273
00:18:58,220 --> 00:18:59,555
Nothing yet, Papa.

274
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:05,519
If you're so proud of that
90-day governor of yours…

275
00:19:06,186 --> 00:19:07,855
Just accept it, Papa.

276
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:10,983
Governor Mateo Ruiz is the governor

277
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:12,192
and in power right now.

278
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:14,278
And, you? You have nothing left.

279
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:22,161
Oops!

280
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:24,371
You know, Papa? I forgot to say something.

281
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:27,166
You're about to become obsolete.

282
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:29,209
[chuckles]

283
00:19:29,501 --> 00:19:30,711
How dare you!

284
00:19:35,007 --> 00:19:39,344
[somber music playing]

285
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:50,939
-[Anna cries]
-[Jepoy] <i>Anna!</i>

286
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:53,775
[Anna] <i>Jepoy.</i>

287
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:57,321
<i>Jepoy, she's gone, Jepoy. She's gone.</i>

288
00:19:57,404 --> 00:19:59,364
[grunting]

289
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:03,869
<i>She's gone, Jepoy.</i>

290
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:09,249
[Jepoy] <i>Nanny, I couldn't protect you.</i>

291
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:14,630
-[screams]
-[gunshot]

292
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:16,048
[gasps]

293
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:35,317
[foreboding music playing]

294
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:39,529
-[gun cocks]
-Jepoy?

295
00:20:41,114 --> 00:20:42,157
Jepoy, wait!

296
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,867
What are you going to do with that, huh?!

297
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:44,993
-Hey! Hey! Hey, Anna!
-No!

298
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:45,994
-Be careful with that!
-Jepoy, no!

299
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:47,287
-Give me that!
-Give that back.

300
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:49,790
You know, I should've never
told you about Arnaldo!

301
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:52,167
Well, it's good you did
'cause I'm going to kill him!

302
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:54,461
He's not the same person anymore!

303
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:56,421
Anna, I don't care!

304
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,131
He killed Nanny Carlotta!

305
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:00,509
And, no matter what,
he's still an Ardiente,

306
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:01,551
so give me that.

307
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:03,178
Jepoy, listen to me!

308
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:04,513
If you kill him,

309
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:06,974
then that makes you
no different from them!

310
00:21:11,478 --> 00:21:12,646
[Anna] Is that what you want?

311
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:20,404
Fine, you can have that.

312
00:21:22,239 --> 00:21:24,992
I won't need it to kill the guy, anyway.

313
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:26,326
-Jepoy, wait!
-What now?!

314
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:28,245
I said, wait! Just listen to me!

315
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:31,164
You don't have to hurt Arnaldo.

316
00:21:32,708 --> 00:21:35,877
You can't just let anger
take over your heart, okay?

317
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:39,381
Listen to me. You are not a murderer.

318
00:21:39,464 --> 00:21:40,924
You don't know that, Anna.

319
00:21:42,217 --> 00:21:43,885
Anger's all I have left in me now.

320
00:21:43,969 --> 00:21:45,679
-Jepoy, please.
-I'm sorry.

321
00:21:46,471 --> 00:21:47,848
-Wait--
-Anna!

322
00:21:48,223 --> 00:21:49,224
You know what?

323
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:55,105
This is for Nanny Carlotta.

324
00:21:56,982 --> 00:21:58,150
This is for her.

325
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:01,278
Jepoy!

326
00:22:01,361 --> 00:22:06,366
[dramatic music playing]

327
00:22:11,788 --> 00:22:13,790
I'm sure by now,
you've heard my son's missing.

328
00:22:13,874 --> 00:22:14,958
Yes.

329
00:22:15,042 --> 00:22:16,626
And what are you going to do about it?

330
00:22:17,252 --> 00:22:19,296
And what? Am I supposed
to do something about it?

331
00:22:19,379 --> 00:22:21,423
Yes! Since you're the governor,

332
00:22:21,506 --> 00:22:24,426
you should be concerned
about the Ardientes' welfare.

333
00:22:31,391 --> 00:22:34,728
Linda, call the chief of police
and tell him

334
00:22:34,811 --> 00:22:38,190
to prioritize the search
for Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.

335
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:45,989
Thank you.

336
00:22:46,073 --> 00:22:48,075
I knew you wouldn't say no to me.

337
00:22:52,287 --> 00:22:55,916
[foreboding music playing]

338
00:22:58,710 --> 00:22:59,753
[birds chirp]

339
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:10,138
[inhales]

340
00:23:10,472 --> 00:23:12,307
[exhales]

341
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:23,401
[tense music playing]

342
00:23:29,116 --> 00:23:30,117
Arnaldo!

343
00:23:30,617 --> 00:23:31,493
You bastard!

344
00:23:31,576 --> 00:23:32,869
[grunts]

345
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:34,704
-Why did you hurt Anna?
-I don't know--

346
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:36,498
-What did I ever do to you?
-I don't know you.

347
00:23:36,581 --> 00:23:38,667
Why do you keep hurting the people I love?

348
00:23:40,127 --> 00:23:41,586
-What's with you?!
-I don't know you.

349
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:43,213
-I don't--
-You don't know me?

350
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:45,465
[grunting]

351
00:23:47,008 --> 00:23:48,260
I'm going to kill you!

352
00:23:51,346 --> 00:23:53,056
I don't know what you're talking about!

353
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,099
Trust me, I'm clueless.

354
00:23:54,182 --> 00:23:57,978
-Please stop!
-[both grunting]

355
00:23:59,521 --> 00:24:00,438
[Jepoy] This is for Nanny Carlotta!

356
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:01,690
[Diego] Jepoy!

357
00:24:04,818 --> 00:24:05,861
[Jepoy] Let go of me!

358
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:09,114
-Stop it!
-Get lost, Diego!

359
00:24:09,948 --> 00:24:11,032
-Hold on!
-I'll kill him!

360
00:24:11,116 --> 00:24:13,243
Hold on! Can you please calm down?!

361
00:24:13,326 --> 00:24:14,953
That man is a murderer!

362
00:24:15,036 --> 00:24:16,913
And his time is up!
It's time to make him pay!

363
00:24:16,997 --> 00:24:19,958
-But we're not murderers!
-Well, he is!

364
00:24:20,792 --> 00:24:22,878
-He's a murderer!
-That's enough, Jepoy!

365
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:26,798
[suspenseful music playing]

366
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:29,634
-[Arnaldo] Enough! Stop! Stop!
-I'll kill you!

367
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:31,678
-Stop it, Jepoy!
-[Jepoy groans]

368
00:24:31,761 --> 00:24:33,889
I'm begging you. Please stop!

369
00:24:35,265 --> 00:24:36,892
I don't know what you're talking about.

370
00:24:36,975 --> 00:24:38,351
[Jepoy grunts]

371
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:40,270
I don't know what you're talking about.

372
00:24:40,353 --> 00:24:42,480
You don't know?!
You killed our Nanny Carlotta!

373
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:43,940
I don't know anything! Believe me.

374
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:48,653
Forgive me for whatever
I did to you, to all of you.

375
00:24:48,737 --> 00:24:51,072
I don't know anything! Forgive me!

376
00:24:51,156 --> 00:24:52,449
Jepoy, enough.

377
00:24:52,532 --> 00:24:54,409
[Arnaldo] I don't know
what you're talking about!

378
00:24:54,492 --> 00:24:55,493
Enough!

379
00:24:55,994 --> 00:24:57,245
I don't remember anything.

380
00:24:57,621 --> 00:25:00,916
I don't remember if I did anything to you.

381
00:25:00,999 --> 00:25:02,500
-You liar!
-Forgive me.

382
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:04,461
Please, forgive me. I'm begging you.

383
00:25:04,544 --> 00:25:08,215
-Diego, he's lying.
-If I did anything to you,

384
00:25:08,298 --> 00:25:12,219
I wholeheartedly ask for your forgiveness.

385
00:25:14,888 --> 00:25:17,933
I really don't remember anything.

386
00:25:29,277 --> 00:25:31,655
Search every corner of Ardiente.

387
00:25:31,738 --> 00:25:33,949
Find Arnaldo.

388
00:25:34,574 --> 00:25:35,659
-Yes, boss.
-Yes, boss.

389
00:25:35,742 --> 00:25:37,327
-Go.
-Let's go.

390
00:25:42,707 --> 00:25:44,376
-Jaguar.
-Emilia.

391
00:25:44,459 --> 00:25:46,544
I've just dispatched my men.

392
00:25:47,629 --> 00:25:50,006
I had them scour Poblacion Ardiente

393
00:25:50,090 --> 00:25:52,175
to find your son, Arnaldo.

394
00:25:52,259 --> 00:25:53,260
Oh!

395
00:25:53,343 --> 00:25:54,886
I didn't know you were up to date

396
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:56,721
with the news in Ardiente.

397
00:25:57,430 --> 00:26:01,142
You know I'm always informed
about Ardiente.

398
00:26:02,102 --> 00:26:04,312
Especially about your life.

399
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:06,898
Aw, Jaguar!

400
00:26:06,982 --> 00:26:10,110
But there seems to be a delay
in your news feed.

401
00:26:10,193 --> 00:26:12,445
Because somebody else
is doing that for me now.

402
00:26:12,529 --> 00:26:13,947
It's Governor Ruiz.

403
00:26:14,030 --> 00:26:17,242
But still, I thank you for your
help. I appreciate it.

404
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:19,744
Hold on.

405
00:26:22,622 --> 00:26:25,750
What is it you admire
about that governor, anyway?

406
00:26:26,376 --> 00:26:27,502
First of all,

407
00:26:27,585 --> 00:26:31,131
he's just Lily Cruz's lapdog, isn't he?

408
00:26:31,214 --> 00:26:32,882
That's what you think.

409
00:26:33,550 --> 00:26:34,801
What you don't know…

410
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:38,430
is that Governor Ruiz has a new master.

411
00:26:38,513 --> 00:26:40,056
And you're in front of her.

412
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:41,683
[chuckles lightly]

413
00:26:41,766 --> 00:26:44,436
But, you know, I believe
in equality among pets.

414
00:26:44,519 --> 00:26:46,813
So, I'll let you fight among yourselves.

415
00:26:46,896 --> 00:26:48,606
Cats versus dogs.

416
00:26:49,316 --> 00:26:51,443
Bye, kitty-kitty. Meow!

417
00:26:51,526 --> 00:26:54,946
Oops! I'm sorry. I mean, Jaguar. Bye-bye!

418
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:07,876
[Jepoy] Why do you keep butting…

419
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:09,085
-into everything?
-Jepoy…

420
00:27:09,169 --> 00:27:10,545
-Jepoy! Why are you fighting?
-Huh?

421
00:27:10,628 --> 00:27:12,255
[Jepoy] And how could you believe him?!

422
00:27:12,339 --> 00:27:14,174
-Don't believe him!
-Why are you arguing?

423
00:27:14,257 --> 00:27:16,134
He's just pretending not to remember,

424
00:27:16,217 --> 00:27:17,635
-but he knows every--
-Jepoy.

425
00:27:18,970 --> 00:27:21,639
What is this? What's going on?

426
00:27:22,599 --> 00:27:23,892
Why are you fighting?

427
00:27:23,975 --> 00:27:24,768
Tell her.

428
00:27:25,602 --> 00:27:26,644
Tell her what you did!

429
00:27:27,896 --> 00:27:28,897
Tell her!

430
00:27:33,401 --> 00:27:35,904
I was about to get rid of Arnaldo…

431
00:27:36,404 --> 00:27:37,614
when he got in the way.

432
00:27:37,697 --> 00:27:40,617
I was this close, Diego! This close!

433
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:44,371
Arnaldo? How did you even get near him?

434
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:47,874
[tense music playing]

435
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:56,549
[Mercedes] We've found your son, Arnaldo.

436
00:27:56,966 --> 00:27:58,051
Is he safe?

437
00:27:58,760 --> 00:27:59,677
Yes.

438
00:27:59,761 --> 00:28:02,931
He's under the care
of the Sitio Onse residents.

439
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:04,682
Yuck!

440
00:28:04,766 --> 00:28:07,477
How can he be safe there
with the poor people?

441
00:28:07,852 --> 00:28:12,732
There's no AC at Sitio Onse.
Mosquitoes will swarm him there!

442
00:28:12,816 --> 00:28:15,193
You have nothing to worry about.

443
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:16,986
Well, if you say so.

444
00:28:18,071 --> 00:28:19,531
But how did you do that?

445
00:28:19,614 --> 00:28:21,533
Is it because of Governor Mateo?

446
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:24,702
No, Emilia.

447
00:28:25,703 --> 00:28:28,248
We already knew where Arnaldo was

448
00:28:28,331 --> 00:28:30,667
before you even spoke to Governor Ruiz.

449
00:28:31,626 --> 00:28:33,586
Hmm? How did that happen?

450
00:28:33,670 --> 00:28:37,882
Papa, Mateo, and even
the Jaguar just started.

451
00:28:37,966 --> 00:28:40,009
Because your mother doesn't
belong in the same league

452
00:28:40,093 --> 00:28:41,052
as those boys.

453
00:28:42,178 --> 00:28:44,347
They are all playing in the playground,

454
00:28:44,431 --> 00:28:46,933
while your mother owns it.

455
00:28:51,896 --> 00:28:52,897
Hmm…

456
00:28:53,314 --> 00:28:55,984
Does that mean I get
to own the playground too?

457
00:28:56,484 --> 00:28:59,904
Of course. You are the heir to the throne.

458
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:02,866
[laughing]

459
00:29:02,949 --> 00:29:05,326
I now love my Mama so much.

460
00:29:10,331 --> 00:29:13,418
[ominous music playing]

461
00:29:13,501 --> 00:29:15,670
Stop staring at each other!
I asked a question!

462
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:17,672
[tense music playing]

463
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,257
He was at Sitio Onse.

464
00:29:19,716 --> 00:29:21,301
I saw him the other day.

465
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:24,721
You saw Arnaldo the other day,
and you didn't tell me?

466
00:29:24,804 --> 00:29:26,890
Lily, I didn't want to add
to all the problems--

467
00:29:26,973 --> 00:29:28,558
That I already have?

468
00:29:28,641 --> 00:29:30,727
With a secret
that could cost you your life?

469
00:29:30,810 --> 00:29:33,271
But it was Arnaldo
who almost died, not me!

470
00:29:33,354 --> 00:29:35,857
And I would've killed him
if you didn't stop me, Diego!

471
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:37,525
He would've been one problem gone!

472
00:29:37,609 --> 00:29:40,361
No matter what you say,
Arnaldo's still my brother!

473
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:42,572
How many times do I have to
say that we're not criminals…

474
00:29:42,655 --> 00:29:44,532
-like them!
-Your brother's a murderer!

475
00:29:44,991 --> 00:29:46,534
And as long as the Ardientes are around,

476
00:29:46,618 --> 00:29:47,911
our lives are in danger, Diego!

477
00:29:47,994 --> 00:29:50,497
If we don't get ahead of them,
they'll wipe us out!

478
00:29:50,872 --> 00:29:52,207
Use your head! Don't be so naïve!

479
00:29:52,290 --> 00:29:54,918
We are not murderers, Jepoy.

480
00:29:56,252 --> 00:29:57,712
I already told you that.

481
00:29:58,880 --> 00:30:01,299
It must've slipped your mind,
so let me repeat it again.

482
00:30:01,966 --> 00:30:04,135
We are not murderers.

483
00:30:04,219 --> 00:30:06,638
If you kill even just
one of the Ardientes,

484
00:30:06,721 --> 00:30:08,431
we will forever have their blood smeared

485
00:30:08,515 --> 00:30:11,017
on our hands and conscience.

486
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:14,646
So I hope you get it now.

487
00:30:24,113 --> 00:30:27,283
-Are you sure Arnaldo's here?
-Yes, Papa.

488
00:30:27,617 --> 00:30:30,662
According to my reliable source,
he is really here.

489
00:30:30,745 --> 00:30:32,747
-Reliable source or gossip?
-Huh?

490
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:34,457
I'm telling you, Emilia.

491
00:30:35,333 --> 00:30:39,128
If you brought me here
only to find nothing,

492
00:30:39,712 --> 00:30:41,297
you're going to be in trouble!

493
00:30:43,508 --> 00:30:45,218
-[Emilia sighs]
-What kind of place is this?

494
00:30:47,220 --> 00:30:51,099
[tense music playing]

495
00:31:01,651 --> 00:31:03,152
Holy sh--

496
00:31:04,654 --> 00:31:06,155
[Julio] What is this?!

497
00:31:07,115 --> 00:31:08,408
Arnaldo?

498
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:10,451
What happened to you?

499
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:11,870
Why do you have--

500
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,079
Did someone beat you up?

501
00:31:13,162 --> 00:31:14,581
[stutters] No.

502
00:31:15,331 --> 00:31:18,042
I just fell over. It was an accident.

503
00:31:18,710 --> 00:31:21,045
You have to come home with us.
You are not safe here.

504
00:31:22,422 --> 00:31:24,465
-I won't come with you.
-Huh?

505
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:28,636
I won't be safer with any of you.

506
00:31:29,721 --> 00:31:31,055
What do you mean?

507
00:31:33,975 --> 00:31:35,977
I found out about your crimes, Grandpa.

508
00:31:41,941 --> 00:31:43,401
All the things you did to the people

509
00:31:43,484 --> 00:31:44,903
of Poblacion Ardiente.

510
00:31:44,986 --> 00:31:48,156
[Julio] What is happening to you?!

511
00:31:48,239 --> 00:31:49,240
Are you even my grandson?!

512
00:31:49,324 --> 00:31:50,241
-Papa!
-Papa!

513
00:31:50,325 --> 00:31:51,242
-Hold on.
-Papa!

514
00:31:51,326 --> 00:31:53,286
No matter what you say,
I'm not going with you!

515
00:31:54,203 --> 00:31:56,456
I was led here to fulfill a mission.

516
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:58,041
I can't just leave.

517
00:31:58,124 --> 00:32:00,460
Like it or not, you're coming with us.

518
00:32:00,543 --> 00:32:04,047
I'll even have my men drag you
away from here if I have to.

519
00:32:04,130 --> 00:32:05,757
Papa, enough, okay? Let him be.

520
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:07,842
If he wants to stay here, then go ahead.

521
00:32:07,926 --> 00:32:10,428
Can't you see even the sky's
getting angry?

522
00:32:10,887 --> 00:32:14,223
Now you're afraid of a
little thunder and lightning?

523
00:32:14,307 --> 00:32:16,225
Wait. Arnaldo, are you
going to be fine here?

524
00:32:16,309 --> 00:32:18,061
-[thunder rumbling]
-I am.

525
00:32:18,144 --> 00:32:21,230
All right. If, or when,
you decide to come home,

526
00:32:21,314 --> 00:32:23,149
we're just one call away, okay?

527
00:32:23,566 --> 00:32:26,152
[pensive music playing]

528
00:32:30,490 --> 00:32:33,368
[Julio] Going up here was a waste of time.

529
00:32:33,451 --> 00:32:36,663
Arnaldo, are you sure
you'll be all right here?

530
00:32:36,746 --> 00:32:38,748
-[Julio speaking indistinctly]
-Yes, I'll be okay.

531
00:32:40,249 --> 00:32:41,626
Take care of yourself, okay?

532
00:32:42,585 --> 00:32:44,003
-All right.
-Thanks.

533
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:50,176
[Julio] Did you hear him?

534
00:32:50,259 --> 00:32:51,177
[Emilia] Yeah.

535
00:32:51,260 --> 00:32:54,973
[somber music playing]

536
00:33:03,147 --> 00:33:04,649
[Anna] Jepoy, sit down.

537
00:33:09,570 --> 00:33:11,364
-Give me your hand.
-[winces]

538
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:14,534
That hurts!
Are you doing that on purpose?!

539
00:33:15,618 --> 00:33:16,661
Jepoy.

540
00:33:20,957 --> 00:33:24,877
I bet Julio already knows
that Arnaldo's at Sitio Onse.

541
00:33:26,087 --> 00:33:29,841
I got a text from the residents
saying they saw Julio,

542
00:33:29,924 --> 00:33:31,968
but that Arnaldo didn't go with them.

543
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:39,726
I'm sure they'll force Arnaldo
to go with them soon enough.

544
00:33:42,770 --> 00:33:44,564
It's all up to him.

545
00:33:46,232 --> 00:33:49,027
But then, the Ardientes' enemies
might still go after him.

546
00:33:49,777 --> 00:33:53,531
I was thinking that maybe
we should help him out.

547
00:33:53,614 --> 00:33:54,991
Protect him, even.

548
00:33:55,366 --> 00:33:56,325
Wait.

549
00:33:56,409 --> 00:33:59,454
Did I hear that right?
We're going to protect Arnaldo?

550
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:03,416
Jepoy, I know it's hard to accept,

551
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:05,835
but what if he's really changed?

552
00:34:06,169 --> 00:34:07,795
He killed Nanny Carlotta.

553
00:34:08,421 --> 00:34:11,799
So, even Emilia and Julio
can be our friends now?

554
00:34:12,383 --> 00:34:14,135
Well then, why not just
invite them all here?!

555
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:15,219
For a chat!

556
00:34:17,055 --> 00:34:18,473
[phone ringing]

557
00:34:18,556 --> 00:34:20,391
[foreboding music playing]

558
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:25,480
[ringing continues]

559
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:31,694
Hello?

560
00:34:34,447 --> 00:34:35,698
Miss Lily Cruz.

561
00:34:36,491 --> 00:34:39,118
Word on the grapevine
is you're looking for me.

562
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:43,956
Mercedes Palacio.

563
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:46,667
[tense music playing]

564
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,378
Yes.

565
00:34:49,462 --> 00:34:50,546
Unfortunately,

566
00:34:50,630 --> 00:34:52,673
<i>this is the closest</i>
<i>you can get to meeting me.</i>

567
00:34:53,382 --> 00:34:56,010
You see, I'm not fond of meeting traitors.

568
00:34:57,053 --> 00:35:00,014
So, is that why you had
all my buildings bombed?

569
00:35:00,848 --> 00:35:01,849
Yes!

570
00:35:02,183 --> 00:35:05,228
And if you don't stop
harassing the Ardientes,

571
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:08,940
I assure you, your loved ones
will be in grave danger.

572
00:35:10,358 --> 00:35:11,734
Mercedes…

573
00:35:12,527 --> 00:35:15,488
<i>I don't think you really know</i>
<i>just who I am.</i>

574
00:35:16,656 --> 00:35:18,783
I've been to hell and back.

575
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:22,495
So there's no way
I'll ever be afraid of you.

576
00:35:22,578 --> 00:35:25,289
[tense music swelling]

577
00:35:41,514 --> 00:35:45,143
I can't believe
that we left Arnaldo there.

578
00:35:45,852 --> 00:35:48,479
The lightning, Papa. It would've struck.

579
00:35:48,563 --> 00:35:52,316
You know, this is why your son
ended up like this.

580
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:53,401
You're weak!

581
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:56,237
A little trouble, you scream!

582
00:35:56,529 --> 00:35:58,823
A little obstacle
and you pull back right away!

583
00:35:59,365 --> 00:36:01,325
I can stand in the center of this field

584
00:36:01,409 --> 00:36:03,536
with thunder and lightning going off,

585
00:36:03,619 --> 00:36:05,872
and not one lightning bolt will touch me.

586
00:36:05,955 --> 00:36:07,623
Even lightning is scared of me.

587
00:36:08,249 --> 00:36:10,501
You know, Papa, this is all your fault.

588
00:36:11,210 --> 00:36:13,379
If only you were a good grandfather,

589
00:36:13,462 --> 00:36:15,923
then Arnaldo wouldn't
have chosen to stay behind.

590
00:36:16,591 --> 00:36:17,550
I knew it.

591
00:36:17,633 --> 00:36:19,886
Out of all the things
you could've inherited

592
00:36:19,969 --> 00:36:21,679
from your arrogant mother,

593
00:36:22,305 --> 00:36:25,766
it just had to be her thick, empty skull.

594
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:27,685
Don't insult my mother.

595
00:36:28,102 --> 00:36:30,938
What is it to you if I do?

596
00:36:33,774 --> 00:36:36,152
[Julio] You look like her,
you think like her.

597
00:36:37,236 --> 00:36:38,321
[sighs]

598
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:52,585
And here's another idiot!

599
00:36:53,252 --> 00:36:54,086
What is it?

600
00:36:57,715 --> 00:37:01,177
[tense music playing]

601
00:37:15,942 --> 00:37:17,693
What is this?

602
00:37:18,527 --> 00:37:20,947
It's simple, Julio Ardiente.

603
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:22,949
I'm letting you know

604
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:25,826
that you no longer have power
over this town.

605
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:29,997
Only your name remains in this place.

606
00:37:35,169 --> 00:37:40,132
And if you are a real man,
you should at least fight fair,

607
00:37:40,216 --> 00:37:43,427
instead of bombing my businesses.

608
00:37:43,511 --> 00:37:44,679
Whoa!

609
00:37:45,304 --> 00:37:51,310
Miss Ivy Aguas, or Lily Cruz,
or whoever you are today,

610
00:37:52,228 --> 00:37:55,731
I may be utterly entertained
by the thought

611
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:59,277
that your businesses
are going up in flames,

612
00:38:00,569 --> 00:38:03,030
but I have nothing to do with that.

613
00:38:03,739 --> 00:38:06,075
-[Julio] I am not behind it all.
-I'm not stupid!

614
00:38:06,158 --> 00:38:09,161
[tense music continues]

615
00:38:09,245 --> 00:38:12,540
I believe that at least
one of you Ardientes

616
00:38:12,623 --> 00:38:15,584
had something to do with
the bombings of my businesses.

617
00:38:16,836 --> 00:38:18,045
Just to remind you,

618
00:38:18,129 --> 00:38:20,756
and to make sure you never forget.

619
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:23,009
You know how I fight.

620
00:38:23,592 --> 00:38:25,928
I never back down.

621
00:38:26,012 --> 00:38:29,765
[dramatic music swelling]

622
00:38:43,112 --> 00:38:46,449
Papa, how are we going
to pass through right now?

623
00:38:46,532 --> 00:38:48,159
She left those barricades.

624
00:38:49,035 --> 00:38:50,077
That's easy.

625
00:38:50,911 --> 00:38:51,954
Let her leave.

626
00:38:52,663 --> 00:38:56,375
Let her take her trained
swinging monkeys with her.

627
00:39:03,132 --> 00:39:05,217
<i>Let us talk about Aguas Realty.</i>

628
00:39:05,718 --> 00:39:07,178
<i>Have you seen the headline about it?</i>

629
00:39:07,261 --> 00:39:09,930
<i>Yes, but as far as Aguas Realty</i>
<i>is concerned,</i>

630
00:39:10,014 --> 00:39:11,307
<i>that's yesterday's news.</i>

631
00:39:11,390 --> 00:39:12,641
<i>Before the market closed,</i>

632
00:39:12,725 --> 00:39:14,894
<i>Aguas Realty's stock went up</i>
<i>five points.</i>

633
00:39:15,519 --> 00:39:16,771
<i>That's pretty awesome.</i>

634
00:39:16,854 --> 00:39:19,607
<i>But how can that happen</i>
<i>within the last 24 hours?</i>

635
00:39:19,690 --> 00:39:22,443
<i>Well, it is because</i>
<i>of their CEO, Miss Lily Cruz.</i>

636
00:39:22,526 --> 00:39:24,820
<i>Her immediate response</i>
<i>and fearless leadership</i>

637
00:39:24,904 --> 00:39:26,864
<i>assured the investors' confidence</i>

638
00:39:26,947 --> 00:39:29,283
<i>that all security issues</i>
<i>have been addressed.</i>

639
00:39:29,367 --> 00:39:31,243
<i>-She's really amazing.</i>
<i>-Yes.</i>

640
00:39:33,162 --> 00:39:36,624
I didn't expect Lily Cruz
to recover so quickly.

641
00:39:40,711 --> 00:39:43,756
But don't worry, Madam.
We're working on it.

642
00:39:43,839 --> 00:39:45,883
[phone ringing]

643
00:39:45,966 --> 00:39:47,760
I'll get back to you as soon as I can.

644
00:39:54,642 --> 00:39:56,519
Julio and the Ardientes

645
00:39:56,602 --> 00:40:00,481
really don't seem to know
about Mercedes Palacio.

646
00:40:02,691 --> 00:40:03,609
[phone ringing]

647
00:40:10,116 --> 00:40:11,033
Hello?

648
00:40:11,492 --> 00:40:15,955
Miss Cruz, I'm calling
to announce your defeat.

649
00:40:16,664 --> 00:40:18,916
<i>You'll never find me.</i>

650
00:40:18,999 --> 00:40:21,127
I've covered my tracks.

651
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:24,964
And you never know
when I'm going to strike next.

652
00:40:25,965 --> 00:40:27,758
So, do you concede?

653
00:40:29,051 --> 00:40:30,052
Never.

654
00:40:35,975 --> 00:40:37,309
That woman…

655
00:40:38,227 --> 00:40:42,815
She really did erase any clues
as to where I can find her.

656
00:40:43,941 --> 00:40:45,609
But I won't stop.

657
00:40:46,527 --> 00:40:47,903
I know I'll find her.

658
00:40:48,779 --> 00:40:54,243
Lily, she forgot one thing.
Mylar's still in police custody.

659
00:40:54,326 --> 00:40:56,579
[tense music swelling]

660
00:41:09,675 --> 00:41:10,968
[Mercedes] Emilia.

661
00:41:12,052 --> 00:41:13,137
The time has come.

662
00:41:15,055 --> 00:41:17,266
Your real mother wants to see you.

663
00:41:17,892 --> 00:41:20,853
[suspenseful music playing]

664
00:41:23,314 --> 00:41:25,816
[ethereal music playing]

665
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:32,323
Hmm.

666
00:41:36,076 --> 00:41:41,207
Is this an early Christmas gift?

667
00:41:43,250 --> 00:41:44,418
My!

668
00:41:46,295 --> 00:41:48,005
Thank you, whoever you are.

669
00:41:50,424 --> 00:41:51,717
[eerie music]

670
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:52,760
[gasps]

671
00:41:55,721 --> 00:41:56,931
Who sent this?!

672
00:42:01,393 --> 00:42:04,522
[ethereal music playing]

673
00:42:34,134 --> 00:42:36,887
Madam, we've delivered
your present for Julio Ardiente.

674
00:42:38,055 --> 00:42:39,098
Excellent.

675
00:42:56,782 --> 00:43:02,121
[ethereal music playing]

676
00:43:42,328 --> 00:43:48,959
[slow music playing]

677
00:45:12,126 --> 00:45:17,214
[slow music continues playing]

678
00:46:13,312 --> 00:46:14,313
[snaps fingers]

679
00:46:14,605 --> 00:46:16,190
[footsteps approaching]

680
00:46:44,176 --> 00:46:47,763
[dramatic music playing]

681
00:47:17,834 --> 00:47:20,963
[somber music playing]

682
00:47:45,612 --> 00:47:46,822
Mama?

683
00:47:47,322 --> 00:47:49,157
Emilia, my daughter.

684
00:48:05,090 --> 00:48:07,134
[sobs] Mama.

685
00:48:15,559 --> 00:48:19,605
[Lily] <i>Red Dragon is the head</i>
<i>of the biggest prostitution,</i>

686
00:48:19,688 --> 00:48:22,941
<i>smuggling, white slavery,</i>
<i>kidnap-for-ransom,</i>

687
00:48:23,025 --> 00:48:25,652
<i>and terrorist syndicate</i>
<i>here in the Philippines.</i>

688
00:48:25,736 --> 00:48:29,781
<i>But I can't understand</i>
<i>why she'd come after me.</i>

689
00:48:29,865 --> 00:48:33,035
<i>I will eliminate both</i>
<i>your papa and Lily Cruz.</i>

690
00:48:33,118 --> 00:48:34,620
<i>I'll give you back your crown.</i>

691
00:48:34,703 --> 00:48:36,830
<i>You will be the queen of Ardiente.</i>

692
00:48:36,913 --> 00:48:39,082
[Julio] <i>Have you really come back?</i>

693
00:48:39,166 --> 00:48:41,251
<i>Why now?</i>

694
00:48:41,335 --> 00:48:45,505
<i>No one and nothing is gonna</i>
<i>separate us ever again.</i>

695
00:48:45,589 --> 00:48:48,133
<i>And if anyone tries, I will crush them.</i>

696
00:48:48,216 --> 00:48:50,927
[theme music playing]
